    Note over Alice,Network: ═══════════ v6 KEY PROPERTIES ═══════════

    rect rgb(255, 255, 200)
        Note over Alice,Network: 🌟 v6 SATISFACTION-BASED FEATURES:<br/><br/>1. ASYNCHRONOUS EVENT-DRIVEN ARCHITECTURE:<br/>   - All entities operate independently<br/>   - No blocking, no coordination required<br/>   - Publish/subscribe pattern via network<br/>   - Reactive computation (Svelte stores)<br/><br/>2. SEPARATED USER INPUT & DERIVED STATE:<br/>   - Tree structure = user inputs (stable)<br/>   - DerivedStateMap = computed values (reactive)<br/>   - Nodes reference derived state (not contain it)<br/>   - Efficient recomputation on changes<br/><br/>3. BOOTSTRAP WITH RECOGNITION:<br/>   - Start with beliefs about contribution<br/>   - No satisfaction data needed initially<br/>   - Enables cold start<br/><br/>4. ACCEPT/DECLINE MECHANISM:<br/>   - Recipients independently control acceptance<br/>   - Asynchronous, no provider blocking<br/>   - Declined resources return to provider<br/>   - Prevents unwanted accumulation<br/><br/>5. SATISFACTION RATING (Async):<br/>   - Recipients rate over time (hours/days)<br/>   - No blocking on satisfaction<br/>   - Measures actual utility, not belief<br/>   - Creates accountability loop<br/><br/>6. AUTOMATIC LEARNING (Reactive):<br/>   - Satisfaction aggregates up tree (automatic)<br/>   - Future allocations reactively updated<br/>   - High satisfaction → larger share<br/>   - Low satisfaction → smaller share<br/><br/>7. PROVIDER QUALITY SIGNALS:<br/>   - Providers observe their satisfaction ratings<br/>   - Learn which recipients they serve well<br/>   - Can adjust offerings based on feedback<br/><br/>8. CONVERGENCE TO UTILITY:<br/>   - System learns what actually works<br/>   - Not just what people believe works<br/>   - Empirically grounded allocation
    end

    Note over Alice,Network: ═══════════ MATHEMATICAL GUARANTEES ═══════════

    rect rgb(220, 255, 255)
        Note over Alice,Network: ✅ STABILITY PROPERTIES (from test2.md):<br/><br/>1. NO INFINITE LOOPS:<br/>   - Time delay: satisfaction rated after allocation<br/>   - Hierarchical dampening: tree aggregation smooths<br/>   - Per-type damping: prevents oscillation<br/>   - Need caps: bounded allocation<br/>   - Asynchronous timing prevents instant feedback<br/><br/>2. GAMING RESISTANCE:<br/>   - Mutual satisfaction: min(S_A→B, S_B→A)<br/>   - Can't inflate unilaterally<br/>   - Recognition overrides satisfaction (eligibility)<br/>   - Network reputation effects<br/><br/>3. CONVERGENCE:<br/>   - Satisfaction → 0.0-1.0 (bounded)<br/>   - Shares sum to 1.0 (normalized)<br/>   - Allocations ≤ needs (capped)<br/>   - System converges to satisfaction equilibrium<br/><br/>4. SELF-CORRECTION:<br/>   - Poor providers → lower satisfaction → reduced share<br/>   - Good providers → higher satisfaction → increased share<br/>   - System optimizes toward actual utility<br/><br/>5. NO ACCUMULATION:<br/>   - Declined resources return immediately<br/>   - Update law: Need(t+1) = Need(t) - Received(t)<br/>   - Same as v5, now with satisfaction weighting<br/><br/>6. PARALLEL EXECUTION:<br/>   - All entities compute independently<br/>   - No sequential bottlenecks<br/>   - Scales horizontally (more entities = no slowdown)<br/>   - Event-driven = resilient to offline entities
    end

    Note over Alice,Network: ═══════════ ARCHITECTURE SUMMARY ═══════════

    rect rgb(230, 230, 250)
        Note over Alice,Network: 🏗️ v6 PARALLEL, EVENT-DRIVEN ARCHITECTURE:<br/><br/>📍 KEY INSIGHT:<br/>User inputs and derived values exist in SEPARATE,<br/>PARALLEL data structures.<br/><br/>🌲 TREE (User Inputs - Stable):<br/>  - Points, contributors, needs, capacities<br/>  - Only changes when user explicitly edits<br/>  - Contains REFERENCES to derived state<br/>  - Serializable, immutable structure<br/><br/>📊 DERIVED STATE MAP (Computed - Reactive):<br/>  - Weights, shares, satisfaction, allocations<br/>  - Recomputes automatically on changes<br/>  - Keyed by node_id for O(1) lookup<br/>  - Ephemeral, can be reconstructed<br/><br/>🔄 REACTIVE FLOW:<br/>  1. User edits tree (user input)<br/>  2. Tree published to network<br/>  3. Other entities observe change<br/>  4. Derived states recompute (automatic)<br/>  5. DerivedStateMap updated (reactive)<br/>  6. UI updates (Svelte $: reactivity)<br/><br/>📡 NETWORK PATTERN:<br/>  - Publish: Entity publishes state changes<br/>  - Subscribe: Others observe relevant changes<br/>  - No RPC, no blocking, no coordination<br/>  - Eventually consistent<br/><br/>✅ BENEFITS:<br/>  - Scalable: O(entities) not O(entities²)<br/>  - Resilient: Offline entities don't block others<br/>  - Efficient: Only recompute what changed<br/>  - Clear: User inputs separated from calculations<br/>  - Fast: Parallel computation where possible
    end